From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000176 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: add dormant P30E MMU-off wire object

Add the first implementation slice for the reviewed P30E contract: two
independent 2 KiB-aligned slots in a retained bidirectional MMU-off section,
controller-side arm/readback helpers, and MMU-off target claim/publication
primitives with CRC, identity, sequence, and full-range cache ordering.

The feature is default-off, has no production caller, does not modify
secondary_entry, and cannot issue CPU_ON/OFF or publish Linux membership. It is
an experiment-only implementation artifact for Buildbox source review; the
existing MT6797 A72 boot and disable vetoes remain unchanged.

This experiment-only change has no certifying sign-off and is not
submission-ready.
